      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find a number \\( N \\) that satisfies the following conditions:\n1. \\( 50 < N < 100 \\)\n2. \\( N \\) is a multiple of \\( 11 \\)\n3. \\( N \\) is not a multiple of \\( 2 \\)\n4. The sum of the digits of \\( N \\) is a multiple of \\( 3 \\)\n\nLet's analyze each condition step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Identify multiples of 11 between 50 and 100\nThe multiples of 11 in this range are:\n\\[ 55, 66, 77, 88, 99 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Exclude multiples of 2\nFrom the list \\( 55, 66, 77, 88, 99 \\), we need to exclude the multiples of 2:\n- \\( 55 \\) is not a multiple of 2.\n- \\( 66 \\) is a multiple of 2.\n- \\( 77 \\) is not a multiple of 2.\n- \\( 88 \\) is a multiple of 2.\n- \\( 99 \\) is a multiple of 2.\n\nSo, the valid multiples of 11 are:\n\\[ 55, 77, 99 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Check if the sum of the digits is a multiple of 3\nWe will now check the sum of the digits for each of these numbers:\n- For \\( 55 \\):\n  \\[ 5 + 5 = 10 \\]\n  10 is not a multiple of 3.\n\n- For \\( 77 \\):\n  \\[ 7 + 7 = 14 \\]\n  14 is not a multiple of 3.\n\n- For \\( 99 \\):\n  \\[ 9 + 9 = 18 \\]\n  18 is a multiple of 3.\n\nThus, the only number that satisfies all the conditions is \\( 99 \\).\n\nTherefore, Bob's favorite number is \\(\\boxed{99}\\).",
